invariant: INV-14
file: cpu_cfg.h
catches: test/host-builds.sh
reason: cpu_cfg.h's x86-64 set gains CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512, so an
  x86-64 object takes a bit that names arm64's SHA-512 instructions and
  has no path for it, where the ruling is that an object refuses a bit of
  the other architecture and does not ignore it (docs/decisions.md 89 and
  93). On arm64 no test row moves, because that set is unchanged, so the
  catch is the script: it reads the header for both architectures under
  the pinned clang and compares each set with the bits it writes out.

--- old
     CH_CPU_VAES | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 | CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA)
--- new
     CH_CPU_VAES | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 | CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512)
